## Context

Author directive (2026-06-06): every figure in the arXiv preprint
(`slides/manuscript/main.md`) must be in English. Historically figures kept
their generated language (cf. 0356 for the EN slide deck — explicitly
deferred regenerating figures in English).

0446 already did the recognition matrix: `--lang {en,fr}` on
`plot_exp1_matrix`, unsuffixed PDF = EN (preprint-first), `_fr` variant for
the report annex (which cross-references the FR difficulty table).

## Quoi faire

1. Inventory every `![...](...)` figure in main.md; for each, list any
   non-English text (titles, axis labels, legends, annotations, band
   labels). Known suspects: the quality spider
   (`plot_quality_spider_exp1.py`: "Vocabulaire respecté", "Exactitude",
   "Cohérence", ... — entirely French), exp2 figures, regimes scatter.
   `fig_direct_p1_base` already has an English title via `--title` /
   `--fp-label "Unrecognized"` (0438).
2. For each FR figure: follow the 0446 pattern — language-parametric
   script, unsuffixed output EN, `_fr` variant only where the report
   actually includes it (report is internal, "no future": do not produce
   FR variants nobody includes).
3. render.mk wiring, one output per rule; rebuild; visual check of every
   converted figure IN the built manuscript (not just standalone).
4. Adherence guard if cheap: a test greping committed preprint figures'
   text layer for known French label strings would ratchet this.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] No French text in any figure included by main.md (verified on the
      built PDF, figure by figure)
- [ ] Report still builds with the labels its FR prose cross-references
- [ ] `make check-fast` + `pytest -m adherence` green
- [ ] Author flip-through of the rebuilt preprint figures

